# Where the append-only-log union is restated (docs/standards/architecture.md rule 9; #670).
# The list of logs is merge-pr.sh's APPEND_ONLY_LOGS, which overlap-read.sh reads from there; the by-hand rule is review-loop step 5.
owner: .claude/skills/review-loop/SKILL.md
claim: a conflict in an append-only log resolves as a union of changes, never of lines, a deletion on either side is authoritative, and the headings are counted before the rebase; the logs are merge-pr.sh's APPEND_ONLY_LOGS
cite: APPEND_ONLY_LOGS
sweep: \bAPPEND_ONLY_LOGS\b|(?i:append-only[- ]logs?\b)|(?i:union (rule|routine|arithmetic|of changes))|\.claude/ledgers/append-only-log-union\.ledger
